<title>USA: CRP rules to be announced Wednesday at 1100 EST.</title>
<headline>CRP rules to be announced Wednesday at 1100 EST.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Agriculture Secretary Dan Glickman will announce the new operating rules for the Conservation Reserve Program at a news conference at 1100 EST/1600 GMT on Wednesday, the department said.</p>
<p>The reserve, which was created in 1985, is the largest long-term land idling program ever. It pays farmers an annual rent to hold fragile land out of production for 10 years. There are now over 32 million acres enrolled in the program.</p>
</text>
